/-!
# Finite type subalgebras of a quasi-coherent algebra sheaf

Let `X` be a scheme and `A` a quasi-coherent sheaf of commutative `𝒪_X`-algebras. The finite
type quasi-coherent subalgebras of `A` form a filtered category, with no hypothesis on `X`.
When `X` is quasi-compact and quasi-separated, `A` is the colimit of these subalgebras, with the
canonical inclusions.

## Main results

All in the namespace `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeSubalgebraFiltered`:

* `isFiltered_finiteTypeSubalgebra`: the finite type quasi-coherent subalgebras of `A` form a
  filtered category.
* `nonempty_isColimit_of_affineSections`: `A` is the colimit of its finite type quasi-coherent
  subalgebras as soon as every section over an affine open comes from one of them.
* `nonempty_isColimit_finiteTypeSubalgebraCocone`: for a quasi-compact and quasi-separated `X`,
  `A` is the colimit of its finite type quasi-coherent subalgebras.

## Implementation notes

Filteredness is `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeDominating.isFiltered`, fed with
`Stacks.AlgebraImageSurjective.imageIsQuasicoherent` (the image of a morphism of quasi-coherent
algebra sheaves is quasi-coherent) and `Stacks.AlgebraImageSurjective.imageIsLocallySurjective`
(the corestriction to the image is locally surjective).

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 05JT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05JT)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.RelativeSpec

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeSubalgebraFiltered

/-- The finite type quasi-coherent subalgebras of a quasi-coherent sheaf of commutative
`𝒪_X`-algebras form a filtered category. No hypothesis on `X` is needed.

An upper bound of two subalgebras is the image of the morphism to `A` out of the pushed-forward
structure sheaf of the fibre product of their relative spectra, and the category is nonempty
because it contains the image of the initial algebra sheaf `𝒪_X`. -/
@[stacks 05JT "directedness"]
theorem isFiltered_finiteTypeSubalgebra {X : Scheme.{u}} (A : AlgebraSheaf X)
    (hA : AlgebraSheaf.IsQuasicoherent A) :
    IsFiltered (FiniteTypeSubalgebras.FiniteTypeSubalgebra A) :=
  FiniteTypeDominating.isFiltered (Stacks.AlgebraImageSurjective.imageIsQuasicoherent X)
    (Stacks.AlgebraImageSurjective.imageIsLocallySurjective X) A hA

/-- A quasi-coherent sheaf of commutative `𝒪_X`-algebras is the colimit of its finite type
quasi-coherent subalgebras, with the canonical inclusions, as soon as every section over an
affine open comes from one of them. -/
theorem nonempty_isColimit_of_affineSections {X : Scheme.{u}} (A : AlgebraSheaf X)
    (hA : AlgebraSheaf.IsQuasicoherent A)
    (hsec : ∀ U : X.Opens, IsAffineOpen U → ∀ x : A.right.obj.obj (Opposite.op U),
      ∃ (B : FiniteTypeSubalgebras.FiniteTypeSubalgebra A)
        (y : (B.obj : AlgebraSheaf X).right.obj.obj (Opposite.op U)),
          (B.obj.arrow.right.hom.app (Opposite.op U)) y = x) :
    Nonempty (IsColimit (FiniteTypeSubalgebras.finiteTypeSubalgebraCocone A)) :=
  have := isFiltered_finiteTypeSubalgebra A hA
  FiniteTypeSubalgebras.nonempty_isColimit_finiteTypeSubalgebraCocone_of_affineSections A hsec

/-- On a quasi-compact and quasi-separated scheme, a quasi-coherent sheaf of commutative
`𝒪_X`-algebras is the colimit of the canonical diagram of its finite type quasi-coherent
subalgebras, with the inclusions of the subobjects as the structure morphisms.

The affine sections hypothesis of `nonempty_isColimit_of_affineSections` is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SubalgebraGeneratedByModule.exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_section`: a
section over an affine open lies in the subalgebra generated by a finite type quasi-coherent
submodule. -/
@[stacks 05JT "the colimit", ega "I 9.6.6" "partial"]
theorem nonempty_isColimit_finiteTypeSubalgebraCocone {X : Scheme.{u}} [CompactSpace X]
    [QuasiSeparatedSpace X] (A : AlgebraSheaf X) (hA : AlgebraSheaf.IsQuasicoherent A) :
    Nonempty (IsColimit (FiniteTypeSubalgebras.finiteTypeSubalgebraCocone A)) :=
  nonempty_isColimit_of_affineSections A hA fun U hU x =>
    SubalgebraGeneratedByModule.exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_section A hA U hU x

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeSubalgebraFiltered

end
